**Definition 1.4 (a common reached prefix and an old target).** Let $P$ be any authentic outer Ready reached from Assumption 1.2's initialization by a finite sequence of returning canonical source cycles and accepted or complete rejected history cycles. Let $c_*$ be the actual cardinality of its immutable cover list. In particular, $P$ may be the first Ready, where $c_*=0$. It may also follow any finite lawful Reserve/Raise/source/history prefix permitted by GCA Theorem 7.2.

The fixed old target core is

$$
D_a=(h_{\le a},X_a),
$$

the actual prefix through stationary acquisition and its raw endpoint. This is the decoded historical core inside an Image of cut $a$. A later Image's cover/package numbers, cover endpoint, full selector binding, sender/receiver origins and publication occurrences are outside this core. They remain part of the actual later delivery and are not identified with $D_a$.

